  "status": "PASS",
  "residual": "Actual dependent history spaces H n, normalized time-varying kernels, and a finite common subkernel construct a common evolution dominated by both original evolutions. Its mass is bounded below by initial common mass times the finite retained product; no TV recurrence is assumed. Summable defects yield the genuine infinite product, and generating-ring event approximation extends the resulting prefix bound to the actual whole product laws. Literal equalities identifying their finite-coordinate marginals with the declared dependent evolutions remain explicit. Initial mismatch and zero/unit-defect boundaries are retained. A fixed positive recurring leak is not summable and its retained-mass budget tends only to one; no exact infinite-survival transfer is asserted."
